WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.360
Skyscrapers,

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.480
missiles,

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.960
cigars,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.400
war memorials,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.920
post boxes.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.400
All examples
of the thrusting, virile,

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.000
long-lasting stamina
of male achievement.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.760
And all, uncannily, celebrating
a specific part of the male body.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.800
Phallocentrism is the idea
that the phallus, or the penis,

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.720
is central to the human experience.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.160
Not just the phallus
on its own, of course,

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.400
but, also, that luckiest of people
in the world - an owner of a phallus.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.400
A proper person, a man.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.960
"Why?" asked Sigmund Freud.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.680
Because, obviously,
it's the best part.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.320
Men know it, and women
who disagree are just envious.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.800
They probably secretly
wish they had one too.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.960
Why settle for a fig, he argued,
when you can have a banana,

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.840
or a cucumber,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.840
or a stick of salami.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.400
They actual word "phallocentrism,"
was coined by Welsh psychoanalyst,

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.240
Alfred Ernest Jones.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.680
He was a close friend
and biographer of Freud,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.640
but disagreed with Freud's theory.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.880
If anything, he argued,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.600
his belief that women
were so envious of men's bits

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.280
revealed far more about Freud
than a secret female plot.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.640
"Relax," he told his friend,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.600
"no woman is going to sneak up
and steal your little Sigmund."

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.360
So, he created
the phrase phallocentrism,

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:40.000
to criticise his Austrian friend's
penis-based paranoia.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.080
The phrase was later picked
up by feminists

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.200
to articulate the experience
of living in a patriarchal society

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.200
and its obsession with
the male view, gaze and audience.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.360
The male experience
in our culture is the default,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.960
the home screen, the universal,
the factory setting, they argued.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:05.600
In reaction to this, female artists
began to create their own work

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.760
that articulated
the female experience,

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.760
and created works that celebrate

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.040
the curves of the female
reproductive parts.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.120
They also reclaimed
earlier ancient works of art

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.840
that celebrated female power.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.160
All to remind the Freudians
of this world,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.440
women are perfectly happy
living penis-free lives.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.960
Sometimes a cigar, is just a cigar.

